    eyelink_file = folder_path + "/" + i + ".asc"
    print(eyelink_file)
    raw = mne.io.read_raw_eyelink(eyelink_file) 
    # blink interpolation
    # do blink interpolation before epoching? probably because its preprocessing, need to then somehow save the new raw (what is the output of this?) and use that for epoching?
    # ! operates in place 

    # "The time in seconds before and after a blink to consider invalid and include in the segment to be interpolated over. Default is 0.05 seconds"
    # "During blink periods, eyegaze coordinates are not reported, and pupil size data are 0" --> not NAN !!

    # "We don’t want these blink artifacts biasing our analysis, so we have two options: Drop the blink periods from our data during epoching, or interpolate the missing data during the blink periods."
    # - am I dropping them during epoching at the moment? If yes I need to stop that after interpolation

    # should I change the default buffer (time of interpolation before and after blink) - > in the tutorial they use (0.05, 0.2)

